            <div xml:id="d1444">

                <pb facs="1155" n="1145" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.953/9–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hawthorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-10T12:00:00+08:00">September 10,
                            1949—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 10—4:59 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>493. Lest Department misunderstand certain recent telegrams from ConGen, we
                    hasten assure Department we are not only willing but anxious remain at post so
                    long Department feels usefulness our activities, now largely restricted
                    telegraphic reporting, warrant continued expenditure necessary Government
                    funds.</p>
                <p>Department pass Nanking its discretion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawthorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
